WEBVTT

00:29:58.380 --> 00:30:00.822
a lot of those people won't be helped.

00:30:00.846 --> 00:30:02.695
And then you'll deal with,

00:30:02.719 --> 00:30:05.437
how will they behave for each other?

00:30:05.461 --> 00:30:11.752
One country's vulnerabilities,
another country's opportunities.

00:30:11.776 --> 00:30:16.606
In such times,
this is the case, because --

00:30:16.630 --> 00:30:19.932
You know, Graham Allison

00:30:19.956 --> 00:30:22.641
wrote a book about the Thucydides trap,

00:30:22.665 --> 00:30:24.458
and he reminds us,

00:30:24.482 --> 00:30:26.580
over the last 500 years,

00:30:26.604 --> 00:30:29.529
there have been 16 countries

00:30:29.553 --> 00:30:33.526
in which there's been a rivalry
of an empire challenging another.